  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_005 (rna_only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc, while image_only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208). We have strong evidence that RNA dominates and that scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool is the optimal RNA pipeline. The key remaining uncertainty is whether adding the image modality via fusion provides any complementary signal beyond the already-strong RNA representation. Question tested: config_030 (multimodal, scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly compares against config_005 by adding only the image branch and a simple concat fusion, isolating the marginal contribution of image. Why best next: It uses the already-validated best RNA settings so any performance change is attributable to the image modality and fusion. If it improves, it justifies further investment in multimodal and stronger image encoders; if it does not, it efficiently rules out multimodal as a direction and lets us focus remaining budget on RNA encoder improvements (e.g., scgpt) or aggregation refinements. This is a single-variable change from the current best, making it the most informative use of one experiment."
}

